# Class and spec talk (intent classtalk), class by class (chat audit CORPUS-C-003, 2026-11-18). A player's "is friar good?" or
# "good paladin spec?" is answered only by a line that names the class asked about (AutonomousBotChatCoordinator: "classtalk
# asked"), so every line here names its class. Before, most classes had one fixed remark and twelve had none. Each class
# gets a few remarks, a little spec talk in its 1.65 lines (no numbers, no templates) and a view from the other realms.
# Own-realm lines are @realm; a view of another realm's class is said by the other realms. New writing (see docs/bot-voices).

@kind reply
@intent classtalk
@who *

# ================================ Albion =================================
@realm alb
# ---- armsman ----
armsmen hit hard and never die, what more do you want
polearm armsman for groups, sword and board solo
an armsman with a crossbow is a funny sight
armsman is slow to level but rock solid
spec your armsman in one weapon and shields
# ---- paladin ----
paladin chants carry a whole group
paladins level slow, they are worth it in groups
most paladins go chants and two handed
a paladin keeps the group alive without a single heal spell
paladin with a big shield, the tank everyone wants
# ---- mercenary ----
mercenary dual wield looks great and hits even better
mercs need a good group, then they shine
pick slash or thrust on your merc and stick to it
mercenary is a fun first character
mercs and their two weapons, never gets old
mercenary is all damage, bring a healer
# ---- reaver ----
reavers are the strangest class we have, i love it
flex and soulrending, thats a reaver
reaver soulrending hurts casters a lot
a reaver with a flail is scary up close
reavers are rare, groups like the novelty
reaver is not easy to play well
# ---- scout ----
scouts sit at range and shoot everything
longbow and shields for a scout, then stealth
scouts are great at pulling
a scout solo is slow but safe
scouts get blamed for every arrow in the frontier
scout range is the best part of the class
# ---- infiltrator ----
infiltrators are a blast if you like stealth
critical strike and envenom for an infiltrator
infils level slow in groups, better solo
infiltrator is all about the opener
infils in the frontier hunt casters
# ---- minstrel ----
minstrels bring speed, everyone loves them
minstrel instruments first, the rest after
a minstrel mez saves a lot of groups
minstrels are good at everything and great at nothing
minstrel stealth is handy for getting places
# ---- cleric ----
clerics get a group any time of day
rejuv cleric for groups, smite cleric for soloing
cleric is the rez bot of the realm lol
clerics are slow solo, but never lfg long
enhancement clerics have the best buffs
# ---- friar ----
friars are gimped, everyone says so, nobody listens
staff and rejuv for a friar
a friar can heal, buff and hit, all a bit
friars solo better than clerics
friar is the most fun healer we have
# ---- wizard ----
wizards hit like a truck from range
fire wizard is the usual pick
earth wizards have a nice bolt
ice wizards slow everything down
a wizard dies fast, stay behind the tank
# ---- theurgist ----
theurgists level fast with their pets
earth theurgist pets tank for you
ice theurgist for damage
theurgist is the easiest class to level imo
wind theurgist is the oddball spec
# ---- sorcerer ----
sorcerer pets do the work early on
sorcerers mez and charm, very handy
mind sorcerer for mez, body for damage
a sorc pet can carry you while leveling
sorcerers are a bit gimped solo early on
sorcs are the mezzers of albion
# ---- cabalist ----
cabalists are a solid pick for a first caster
cabalist pets are tough
matter cabalist for the damage over time
body cabalist if you want the direct damage
cabalists solo really well
spirit cabalist is for the brave
cabbies are underrated in groups
# ---- necromancer ----
necromancers are a weird class, you are the pet
painworking necro for damage
deathsight necro for the lifetaps
necro pets hit hard, the necro hides
a necro is slow at first, then it clicks

